title: 'pallet-assets: allow force_create to set an arbitrary asset id when auto-increment is enabled'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `force_create` no longer requires the asset id to equal `NextAssetId`: a `ForceOrigin` may
    create an asset with any id not currently in use, and the id is then marked as allocated so it
    can never later collide. Asset id allocation is now configured explicitly via the new
    `Config::AssetIdAllocator` (`AutoIncAssetId` for auto-incrementing ids, `()` for none),
    replacing the implicit `NextAssetId`-is-`Some` plus `AutoIncAssetId` callback mechanism.
    Only the `force_create` call is relaxed; `fungibles::Create::create` is not gated on
    `ForceOrigin` and still requires the id the allocator dictates.

    Migration: set `AssetIdAllocator` on each `pallet-assets` `Config`. Use `AutoIncAssetId<Runtime, I>`
    where `CallbackHandle` previously used it (and drop it from `CallbackHandle`); otherwise `()`.
    Configs deriving `TestDefaultConfig` inherit `()`.

